---
import { SitePage } from '@boombapbot/editor';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Stay Stoked, Stay Woke · boombapbot"
  description="A footnote to a drum machine made by a white guy in tech, about whose music made drum machines matter."
>
  <SitePage client:load baseUrl={base} current="manifesto" layout="note">
    <h1>Stay Stoked, Stay Woke</h1>
    <p>This is a footnote to a drum machine made by a white guy in tech (me), with a shop attached.</p>
    <p>
      A lot of the reason anyone still cares about drum machines is what Black musicians worked out how to do with
      them. Black artists built house and techno, and you can hear both all weekend without hearing much about the
      people who built them. In hip-hop and dance music, white artists like the Beastie Boys and Diplo built huge
      careers on sounds that Black artists developed.
    </p>
    <p>
      It’s a familiar pattern. Black music, slang and dances travel easily. Meanwhile Black kids get pushed into the
      school-to-prison pipeline, and Black patients struggle to be heard in the health care system.
    </p>
    <p>I love these sounds. I think about all of this whenever I put a price on something here.</p>
  </SitePage>
</Base>
